  "text": "Maqam Saba (not part of a maqam family) Maqam Index Pronunciation of Saba Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Saba is a very popular and common maqam in the Arabic repertory. Its scale starts with Jins Saba on the tonic , overlapped by Jins Hijaz on the 3 rd degree, followed by either Jins ‘Ajam or Jins Nikriz on the 6 th degree. Maqam Saba is not part of a maqam family. Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Saba by Sami Abu Shumays. Dulab, Taqsim Nay & Layai Saba Sabri al-Mudallal al-Atlal (1966) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Huwwa Sahih il-Hawa Ghallab (1960) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) Muwashah Ahwa Qamaran Ghada Shbeir Muwashah Ghuddi Jufunik Khaled al-Hafez Qadd Ya m-as‘ad el-Sabahiyya Sabah Fakhri (Traditional Melody) Tishuf Umuri (1930) Umm Kulthum Music by Muhammad al-Qasabgi (Egypt) Sama‘i Saba Music by Youssef Kassab",
